11
00:50:13,043 --> 00:50:19,043
Prelude to a Kiss is a 1992 American romantic fantasy film directed by Norman
René and starring Alec Baldwin, Meg Ryan, and Sydney Walker.

12
00:54:46,956 --> 00:54:52,956
The movie follows a conservative man, Peter (Baldwin), and a
liberal woman, Rita (Ryan), falling in love.

13
00:59:20,869 --> 00:59:26,869
On their wedding day, Rita (who fears life's uncertainties and is cynical of the world) is kissed
by an elderly stranger named Julius (Walker), causing their souls to switch places.

14
01:03:54,782 --> 01:04:00,782
Peter realizes the change and reunites with Rita,
now in the form of an elderly man.

15
01:08:28,695 --> 01:08:34,695
While trying to figure out how to restore his wife, Peter
tries to connect with Rita despite her new form.

16
01:13:02,608 --> 01:13:08,608
The movie is based on the 1988 play of the same title that was also directed by Norman René
and written by playwright Craig Lucas, who adapted the film's screenplay.

17
01:17:36,521 --> 01:17:42,521
Alec Baldwin and Debra Monk were part of the cast in the play's worldwide premiere in New York City as
well as the film cast, though while Baldwin reprised the same part, Monk played a new role.

18
01:22:10,434 --> 01:22:16,434
The title is taken from the 1938 torch song of the same title by Duke Ellington.

19
01:26:44,347 --> 01:26:50,347
Regarding the movie's story, critic James Hebert wrote: "When it [the play] premiered in
1990, it was widely presumed to be an oblique response to the ravages of AIDS.

20
01:31:18,260 --> 01:31:24,260
Long removed from that time, it becomes a broader commentary on eternal
topics like the limits of love and the meaning of commitment."

21
01:35:52,173 --> 01:35:58,173
The film explores themes of love at first sight,
body exchange, body-swap, body switch.

22
01:40:26,086 --> 01:40:32,086
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
